<h2 class="h3">Utility Methods</h2>

<h3 class="h4">Check if running inside an operation</h3>

<p>
The <code>operation?</code> method returns <code>true</code> if the job is running inside an operation context, <code>false</code> otherwise.<br>
This is useful for writing jobs that can run both with and without operations:
</p>

<pre tabindex="0">
class MyJob < Lato::ApplicationJob
  def perform(params = {})
    save_operation_output_message("Running inside operation") if operation?
    # ... job logic works even without an operation
  end
end
</pre>

<h3 class="h4">Clear operation logs</h3>

<pre tabindex="0">
class MyJob < Lato::ApplicationJob
  def perform(params = {})
    add_operation_log("Step 1 started")
    clear_operation_logs # removes all previous logs
    add_operation_log("Restarted from scratch")
  end
end
</pre>

<h2 class="h3">Operation Query Methods</h2>

<p>
The <code>Lato::Operation</code> model provides several query methods to inspect an operation's state and output:
</p>

<pre tabindex="0">
operation = Lato::Operation.find(id)

# State checks
operation.finished? # returns true if completed or failed

# Output checks
operation.output_message? # returns true if an output message is set
operation.output_message  # returns the output message string

operation.output_action?  # returns true if an output action is set
operation.output_action   # returns the output action hash

operation.output_error?   # returns true if an output error is set
operation.output_error    # returns the output error string

operation.output_file?    # returns true if an output file is attached
</pre>

<h2 class="h3">Maintenance Jobs</h2>

<p>
Lato includes two cleanup jobs. They are not scheduled automatically: schedule them in your application.
</p>

<ul>
  <li><code>Lato::LatoOperationsCleanerJob</code> deletes operations that are not running and are older than 12 hours.</li>
  <li><code>Lato::ActiveStorageCleanerJob</code> purges unattached Active Storage blobs older than 12 hours and removes empty folders of the Disk service. Pass <code>min_age_hours</code> to change the age, e.g. <code>Lato::ActiveStorageCleanerJob.perform_later(min_age_hours: 24)</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Example with Solid Queue recurring tasks:</p>

<pre tabindex="0">
# config/recurring.yml
production:
  lato_operations_cleaner:
    class: Lato::LatoOperationsCleanerJob
    schedule: every day at 3am
  lato_active_storage_cleaner:
    class: Lato::ActiveStorageCleanerJob
    schedule: every day at 4am
</pre>

<p>Without a recurring scheduler, call them from cron:</p>

<pre tabindex="0">
0 3 * * * cd /app && bin/rails runner 'Lato::LatoOperationsCleanerJob.perform_later'
0 4 * * * cd /app && bin/rails runner 'Lato::ActiveStorageCleanerJob.perform_later'
</pre>
